  "description": "Ordinary misery is arranged into perfect tableaux. Fifty short scenes — a psychiatrist who's stopped believing, a girl dreaming of marrying a rock star, a carpet seller, a tuba ruining a marriage — shot in fixed frames of grey-green precision, each a small diorama of someone waiting for life to start. Deadpan as compassion: nobody is mocked, everybody is framed beautifully, nothing is resolved.\n\nHumankind's greatness, baseness, joy, sorrow, self-confidence, anxiety, desire to love and be loved.",
